=== the reds B7 sat beside (unchanged from increment 22) ===
descriptor: B2 (no adopted line), B3 (first read 0x0), B4 (second Copying)
no-fd:      B3 (no read reaches the file class), B4 (no Done)
no-heap:    B4 (no Done), B5 (the #PF inside the withheld page)
7 red total.

=== what each B7 reading means ===
control — the resumed stack is the captured one, and boot 2 went 840 bytes deeper
          than the stop; the checkpoint carried the poison and the writes.
descriptor — the Linux task record was dropped, so no resumed stack exists. The
          restarted child's own teardown DOES produce an exit scan, and it reads
          byte-identically to the control's (3488/57424/0x4000000a9050) because
          it re-runs the same workload from _start; B7 validates that line and
          deliberately does not compare it to the stop.
no-fd —   the adopted tenant exits during the refused read, at exactly the
          depth the stop saw. The monotonic check is >=, not >: a faithful
          restore cannot be shallower than the capture, but it need not go
          deeper.
no-heap — the tenant dies by #PF and leaves through process_exit, whose teardown
          the exit report does not ride. B7 names the missing scan instead of
          passing on it, and still checks the stop line.

=== replaying the recordings ===
tests/e7_gate_check.sh --replay /tmp/e7-gate-teeth-hwm/teeth/<name> returns the same
B7 line for each of the four directories; the control exits 0 as a passing run, and
each tooth exits 0 as a tooth run whose reds are exactly its declared set.
